1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,030
Give a paper strip a half twist —
only one side?

2
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:05,600
Cut a long strip of paper

3
00:00:05,650 --> 00:00:07,350
Give one end a half twist

4
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:10,300
Tape the ends together — done!

5
00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:14,270
Draw a pencil line
down the middle of the strip

6
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:18,840
After one lap…
the line is on the back!

7
00:00:18,890 --> 00:00:21,210
Back to the start after two laps!
Front and back are one single side

8
00:00:21,260 --> 00:00:28,980
What if you cut along this line?

9
00:00:29,030 --> 00:00:31,750
The answer is B! It doesn't split in two

10
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:35,720
One big loop — twice as long,
with two full twists!

11
00:00:35,770 --> 00:00:38,390
It's called a Möbius strip —
use scissors carefully, with an adult!

12
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:40,940
What if you cut one third of the way in?
Try it and tell us in the comments!

13
00:00:40,990 --> 00:00:44,440
NEXT: How many folds
to reach the Moon?
